224-## 4. Workflow JSON schema (frozen)
225-
226:As specified in [proposition-final.md](proposition-final.md) §Persistence — `schema_version: 1`, nodes `{id, type, type_version, name, position, configuration, disabled}`, edges `{id, source_node, source_port, target_node, target_port, edge_type}`, `variables`, `viewport`, `settings: {on_error}`, ISO timestamps. Persisted under `output/workflows/{workflow_id}.json` via `safe_json_write`; soft-delete to `output/TRASH/workflows/`. `output/workflows/` and `output/branding/` must be added to clear-all handling.
227-
228-`sanitize_project_id` is a normalizer, not sufficient request validation: it silently removes
229-invalid characters and can alias two user inputs. API IDs must first match the entire strict
230-pattern `^wf_[A-Z0-9]{6}$` or `^ex_[A-Z0-9]{6}$` as applicable, then be resolved with
231-`safe_join`. Imported node/edge IDs use a documented bounded safe pattern and must also be
232-unique within the document. Reject altered, empty, overlong, wrong-prefix, and duplicate IDs;
233-never normalize them into acceptance.
234-
235-### 4.1 Field-level validation policy
236-
237-The implementation may use Pydantic or equivalent explicit validators, but these constraints
238-are transport-independent:
239-
240-| field | rule |
241-|---|---|
242-| document | JSON object, UTF-8, maximum 2 MiB after encoding, maximum nesting depth 20 |
243-| `schema_version` | required integer, exactly `1` |
244-| `workflow_id` | server-generated on create; otherwise required `^wf_[A-Z0-9]{6}$` |
245-| `name` | required trimmed string, 1–120 characters |
246-| `description` | string, 0–2,000 characters |
247-| `nodes` | required array, 0–200 unique nodes |
248-| `edges` | required array, 0–500 unique edges |
249-| node `id` | `^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,63}$`, unique |
250-| node `type` | required registry key, maximum 80 characters |
251-| node `type_version` | required positive integer supported by the registry |
252-| node `name` | trimmed string, 1–120 characters |
253-| node `position.x/y` | finite number in `[-1000000, 1000000]` |
254-| node `configuration` | JSON object, maximum 256 KiB per node, schema-validated |
255-| node `disabled` | required boolean |
256-| edge `id` | `^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,63}$`, unique |
257-| edge endpoints/ports | existing node IDs and registry port IDs; maximum 64 characters each |
258-| edge `edge_type` | `data` or `control`, and must match the source/target port types |
259:| `variables` | finite JSON object, maximum 64 KiB; expression path segments match `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,63}` |
260-| `viewport` | finite `x/y`; `zoom` in `[0.1, 1.5]` |
261-| `settings.on_error` | `stop` in v1; later values enabled only with Phase 4 capability support |
262-| timestamps | RFC 3339 strings written by the server; clients cannot override them on update |
263-
264-V1 rejects unknown fields at the document, node, and edge levels. Forward-compatible metadata
265-must live under a bounded `extensions` object (reserved now, optional, ignored by execution,
266-round-tripped). This avoids silently trusting misspelled contract fields while leaving an
267-explicit extension path. JSON numbers must be finite; `NaN` and infinities are rejected.
268-
269-### Expressions and data mapping (Phase 5.5)
270-
271:An expression is a string containing exactly one whole-value reference (surrounding whitespace
272-is ignored): `{{ nodes.<node_id>.outputs.<port_id> }}`, `{{ workflow.project_id }}`, or
273:`{{ variables.<name>[.<nested_name>...] }}`. Interpolation, operators, calls, indexing, and
274-all other roots are invalid. Whole-value replacement preserves the referenced JSON type.
275-Expressions may appear recursively in configuration JSON, but structural configuration such as
276-dynamic `port_type` must still resolve to a valid registry value.
277-
278-Node-output references must name an existing non-control output on a strict graph ancestor and
279:that ancestor must be included in the selected execution scope. Static expression validation is
280-part of workflow validation and scheduler construction. Immediately before a node is fingerprinted
281:and invoked, expressions resolve from already-produced outputs, immutable execution `project_id`,
282:and the workflow snapshot's finite JSON `variables`; the resolved configuration is schema-validated.
283-A skipped, absent, or stale output fails with `EXPRESSION_VALUE_UNAVAILABLE`. The parser does not
284-evaluate code and exposes no environment, secret store, object attributes, or filesystem API.
